# Mutation cases for "a `namelist` name that a `<param>` of the same send or invoke
# already names is refused by name" under the C11 lowering
# (docs/SCE_ACCEPTED_SUBSET.md §2.15).
#
# Run with
# `scripts/mutate sce-build/tests/mutations/a_namelist_name_a_param_already_names_is_refused_for_c.cases`.
#
# A `<param>` name that repeats is one array on every engine, which the C writer
# writes by itself as it is given the pairs of a name one after another. Where a
# `namelist` name stands among the `<param>`s that share it is not a document order
# the engines were held to, so the lowering refuses it by name rather than choose
# one. The judge's two cases (`a_namelist_name_that_repeats_a_param_is_refused_for_c`
# and its invoke twin) read the refusal; the case below takes it away:
#
#   a `namelist` name that a `<param>` or an earlier name already names is let through.
#
# Anchors are literal slices of the source; an edit that moves one is reported
# INCONCLUSIVE with the anchor quoted, never as a pass.

mutation_tests -p sce-build --features cli --test a_static_datamodel_holds_every_variable_to_a_type
mutation_targets sce-build/src/forge/static_lowering.rs
mutation_oracles sce-build/tests/a_static_datamodel_holds_every_variable_to_a_type.rs

mutation_case "a namelist name that is already taken is let through" <<'PY'
edit("sce-build/src/forge/static_lowering.rs",
     "    namelist.split_whitespace().find(|name| !seen.insert(*name))",
     "    namelist.split_whitespace().find(|name| !seen.insert(*name) && false)")
PY
